  "PhotoPath": "",
  "Caption": "Exceptions or Result?\n\nExceptions are for the exceptional. When a failure is expected \u2014 not found, invalid input, a rule that didn\u0027t pass \u2014 model it as data and return a Result\u003CT\u003E. The failure lives in the signature, callers must handle it, and you compose without try/catch on the happy path.\n\nStill throw for broken invariants, truly unexpected I/O, or anything this layer can\u0027t sensibly handle.\n\nDo you return Result or throw? Where do you draw the line?\n\n#DotNet #CSharp #CleanCode #SoftwareArchitecture",
